  "premise_review": [
    "StableSphere consists of two optional Nat values and a String label. No sphere space, stable stem group, dimension equation, construction or relationship between the metadata is given.",
    "StableSphereCollapse stores a TMFTorsionFraming, an arbitrary Type sourceCellularBoundary, targetSphere, bare collapseMap Prop and a supplied proof of tmfFraming.trivialized. collapseMap is not a function and has no proof field.",
    "The exact has_target proof is the genuine witness pair C.targetSphere with rfl under the entire C premise. It is recognized and retained, rather than interpreted as constructing a collapse or sphere.",
    "The exact torsion_killed proof projects C.torsionKilled. The TMF context trivialized is a chosen proposition with a supplied proof, without a torsion equation.",
    "The actual equality witness depends on the same-file mixed StableSphereCollapse record. Do not narrow that record, duplicate a provider, or add a missing legacy self-import merely to extract the witness."
  ],
  "conceptual_split_decision": "The independent StableSphere record is descriptive optional metadata only. Preserve it and the complete mixed collapse provider with both genuine proof terms in the archives; the existing imported-provider wrapper is assessed separately at208.",
